{"authored" [{"question" "q-50220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{y}^{2}=0$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-50220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-{y}^{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ -\\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =x+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{x+C}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{x+C},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\frac{1}{1+C} \\\\ 1+C & =1 \\\\ C & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{y}^{2}=0$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-50220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "afe84ab9c69899a72f3968d99750212c45d5146749e48d0ceaee86452fb5b9aa" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-50220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-50220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{1}{2-x}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-50220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{1}{2x-1}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-50220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{1}{x}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-50220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{2}{x+1}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-50220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{2}{x}-1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $y' = 5y$ that satisfies $y(0)=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/example-540.json" "file_sha256" "1a22bc19e61aacd899d91e4ef567556882bdb4398e2c495b8915566861d8da32" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =5\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =5x+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm {e}^{5x+C} \\\\  & =\\pm {e}^{C}{e}^{5x} \\\\  & =K{e}^{5x}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm e^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nNow we apply the condition $y(0) = 3$ to find $K\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =3 \\\\ K{e}^{5\\cdot 0} & =3 \\\\ K & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $y' = 5y$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=3$ is\n\n$$\ny = 3 e^{5x}  \\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/example-540.json" "file_sha256" "1a22bc19e61aacd899d91e4ef567556882bdb4398e2c495b8915566861d8da32" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\cos(3y)\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} + \\sin(2x) = 0$ given that  $y\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0.$ Assume that $-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} < y < \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/example-541.json" "file_sha256" "a5f3e5f03f387c5a545cbc855fc0d68f5d920decc385e2d02bac45f56f99b312" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\,\\text{d}y & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+C \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+{C}_{1}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C_1=3C.$\n\nNow let's apply the condition $y\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0$ to find $C_1\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+{C}_{1} \\\\ 0 & =0+{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\sin(3y)   =  \\dfrac {3} {2} \\cos(2x)\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/example-541.json" "file_sha256" "a5f3e5f03f387c5a545cbc855fc0d68f5d920decc385e2d02bac45f56f99b312" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $3{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{y}^{3}=4x$ that satisfies $y(0)=1.$  Assume that $y>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d2448865aca91aecc19a4b1a66aa5a815bfc865917ae71a92e878d7e28c7c0" "basis" 1194 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{y}^{3} & =4x \\\\ 3{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x(2+{y}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\int \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the integral on the left-hand side of this equality, we use a substitution\n\n$$\nu=2+{y}^{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nThen  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{2+{y}^{3}}(3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+{C}_{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3})+{C}_{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we used that $y>0.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3})+{C}_{2} & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3}) & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1}-{C}_{2} \\\\ {e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3})} & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{C}_{1}-{C}_{2}} \\\\ 2+{y}^{3} & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {y}^{3} & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{{C}_{1}-{C}_{2}}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(0)=1$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}^{3} & =K{e}^{{0}^{2}}-2 \\\\ 1 & =K-2 \\\\ K & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}=3{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d2448865aca91aecc19a4b1a66aa5a815bfc865917ae71a92e878d7e28c7c0" "basis" 1194 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "94228d1cf50b4ffe133be171eee2ad6084302ecd52a10d818f64b11428885957" "basis" 1194 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79425" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d2448865aca91aecc19a4b1a66aa5a815bfc865917ae71a92e878d7e28c7c0" "basis" 1194 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79425" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=2{e}^{x}-1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d2448865aca91aecc19a4b1a66aa5a815bfc865917ae71a92e878d7e28c7c0" "basis" 1194 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79425" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{2}=2{e}^{{x}^{2}}-1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d2448865aca91aecc19a4b1a66aa5a815bfc865917ae71a92e878d7e28c7c0" "basis" 1194 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79425" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{2}=3{e}^{x}-2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d2448865aca91aecc19a4b1a66aa5a815bfc865917ae71a92e878d7e28c7c0" "basis" 1194 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79425" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{3}=3{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d2448865aca91aecc19a4b1a66aa5a815bfc865917ae71a92e878d7e28c7c0" "basis" 1194 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-79425" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{3}={e}^{{x}^{2}}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d2448865aca91aecc19a4b1a66aa5a815bfc865917ae71a92e878d7e28c7c0" "basis" 1194 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028823/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-50566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x$  that satisfies  $y(-3)=1.$  Assume that $y>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-50566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x \\\\ \\int y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\text{d}y & =\\int x\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{C}_{1} \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+2{C}_{1} \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+2{C}_{1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssuming $y>0,$ the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+C},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(-3)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+C} \\\\ 1 & =\\sqrt{9+C} \\\\ C & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x$ that satisfies the condition $y(-3)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-50566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e88c4fa705fe5f93bbdcbe23baa488aa4a8e76a12e3e691a6f6f1f28a24352e5"} {"question" "q-50566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-50566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-y=\\sqrt{2x+7}"] ["math" "-y=\\sqrt{x+4}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-2}"] ["math" "y=\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-4}"] ["math" "y=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-50566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-14313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}$  that satisfies $y(1)=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-14313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ {y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2} \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{3}}{3} & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{C}_{1} \\\\ {y}^{3} & ={x}^{3}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere   $C=3{C}_{1}$ is an arbitrary constant.  \n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)=2$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{3} & ={1}^{3}+C \\\\ 8-1 & =C \\\\ C & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}={x}^{3}+7.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-14313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e88c4fa705fe5f93bbdcbe23baa488aa4a8e76a12e3e691a6f6f1f28a24352e5"} {"question" "q-14313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-14313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}^{3}=2{x}^{3}+2"] ["math" "{y}^{3}=3{x}^{2}+5"] ["math" "{y}^{3}=5{x}^{3}+3"] ["math" "{y}^{3}={x}^{2}+3"] ["math" "{y}^{3}={x}^{3}+7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-14313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{3}={x}^{3}+7"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-8308" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y$  that satisfies $y(0)=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-8308" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =x+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{x+C}\\, \\\\ y & =\\pm {e}^{x+C} \\\\ y & =K{e}^{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=1$ to find $K:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =K{e}^{0} \\\\ K & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{x}\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-8308" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e88c4fa705fe5f93bbdcbe23baa488aa4a8e76a12e3e691a6f6f1f28a24352e5"} {"question" "q-8308" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-8308" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=1"] ["math" "y=x+1"] ["math" "y={e}^{-x}"] ["math" "y={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}"] ["math" "y={e}^{x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-8308" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={e}^{x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-355579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{x}}$  that satisfies $y(1)={e}^{2}.$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-355579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =2\\sqrt{x}+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{2\\sqrt{x}+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{2\\sqrt{x}+C}\\, \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{2\\sqrt{x}}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ y & =K{e}^{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)={e}^{2}$ to find $K:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2} & =K{e}^{2\\sqrt{1}} \\\\ {e}^{2} & =K{e}^{2} \\\\ K & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{x}}$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)={e}^{2}$ is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-355579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e88c4fa705fe5f93bbdcbe23baa488aa4a8e76a12e3e691a6f6f1f28a24352e5"} {"question" "q-355579" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-355579" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e^{2\\sqrt{x}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-50220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{y}^{2}=0$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-50220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-{y}^{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ -\\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =x+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{x+C}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{x+C},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\frac{1}{1+C} \\\\ 1+C & =1 \\\\ C & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{y}^{2}=0$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-50220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e88c4fa705fe5f93bbdcbe23baa488aa4a8e76a12e3e691a6f6f1f28a24352e5"} {"question" "q-50220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-50220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{1}{2-x}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{2x-1}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{x}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{2}{x+1}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{2}{x}-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-50220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{1}{x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-79425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $3{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{y}^{3}=4x$ that satisfies $y(0)=1.$  Assume that $y>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-79425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{y}^{3} & =4x \\\\ 3{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x(2+{y}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\int \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the integral on the left-hand side of this equality, we use a substitution\n\n$$\nu=2+{y}^{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nThen  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{2+{y}^{3}}(3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+{C}_{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3})+{C}_{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we used that $y>0.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3})+{C}_{2} & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3}) & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1}-{C}_{2} \\\\ {e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3})} & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{C}_{1}-{C}_{2}} \\\\ 2+{y}^{3} & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {y}^{3} & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{{C}_{1}-{C}_{2}}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(0)=1$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}^{3} & =K{e}^{{0}^{2}}-2 \\\\ 1 & =K-2 \\\\ K & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}=3{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-79425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e88c4fa705fe5f93bbdcbe23baa488aa4a8e76a12e3e691a6f6f1f28a24352e5"} {"question" "q-79425" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-79425" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=2{e}^{x}-1"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=2{e}^{{x}^{2}}-1"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=3{e}^{x}-2"] ["math" "{y}^{3}=3{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2"] ["math" "{y}^{3}={e}^{{x}^{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-79425" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{3}=3{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-355582" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ given that  $\\,y(0)=0.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-355582" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x}{e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =-{e}^{-x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{0}+C) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-1) & =0 \\\\ C-1 & =1 \\\\ C & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=0$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-{e}^{-x}).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-355582" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e88c4fa705fe5f93bbdcbe23baa488aa4a8e76a12e3e691a6f6f1f28a24352e5"} {"question" "q-355582" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-355582" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ln(2-e^{-x})"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-79371" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{e}^{x}=3$ that satisfies $y(0)=-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-79371" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{e}^{x} & =3 \\\\ {e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3+2x{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{e}^{-x}+2x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{e}^{-x}+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 3{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-3{e}^{-x}+{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(0)=-3$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =-3 \\\\ -3{e}^{-0}+{0}^{2}+C & =-3 \\\\ C-3 & =-3 \\\\ C & =0\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of ${e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{e}^{x}=3$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=-3$ is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}-3{e}^{-x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-79371" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e88c4fa705fe5f93bbdcbe23baa488aa4a8e76a12e3e691a6f6f1f28a24352e5"} {"question" "q-79371" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-79371" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-2{e}^{-x}-1"] ["math" "y=4x+{e}^{-3x}-4"] ["math" "y=x+{e}^{-3x}-4"] ["math" "y={x}^{2}-3{e}^{-x}"] ["math" "y={x}^{2}-3{e}^{-x}+2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-79371" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={x}^{2}-3{e}^{-x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-355564" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $(-\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{2}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4$ that satisfies $y(1)={e}^{2}.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-355564" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{2}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4 \\\\ \\frac{2x-1}{xy}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{4x}{2x-1} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2+\\frac{2}{2x-1} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =(2+\\frac{2}{2x-1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2+\\frac{2}{2x-1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =2x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{2x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{2x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{2x}\\cdot {e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ y & =K(2x-1){e}^{2x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)={e}^{2}$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & ={e}^{2} \\\\ K(2(1)-1){e}^{2(1)} & ={e}^{2} \\\\ K{e}^{2} & ={e}^{2} \\\\ K & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=(2x-1){e}^{2x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-355564" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e88c4fa705fe5f93bbdcbe23baa488aa4a8e76a12e3e691a6f6f1f28a24352e5"} {"question" "q-355564" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-355564" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(2x-1)e^{2x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-350957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{-y}=6{x}^{2}{e}^{-y}$ that satisfies $y(1)=0.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-350957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{-y} & =6{x}^{2}{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6{x}^{2}{e}^{-y}-{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(6{x}^{2}-1){e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =(6{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (6{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =2{x}^{3}-x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{x}^{3}-x+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{x}^{3}-x+C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\cdot {1}^{3}-1+C) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+C) & =0 \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{x}^{3}-x).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-350957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e88c4fa705fe5f93bbdcbe23baa488aa4a8e76a12e3e691a6f6f1f28a24352e5"} {"question" "q-350957" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "q-350957" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ln(2x^3-x)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/state.json" "file_sha256" "6231efa6d8bdd08ae635046da66dc92b893ef06cb29177c449ac99972d24c68e"} {"question" "e-540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $y' = 5y$ that satisfies $y(0)=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/example-540.json" "file_sha256" "1a22bc19e61aacd899d91e4ef567556882bdb4398e2c495b8915566861d8da32"} {"question" "e-540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =5\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =5x+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm {e}^{5x+C} \\\\  & =\\pm {e}^{C}{e}^{5x} \\\\  & =K{e}^{5x}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm e^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nNow we apply the condition $y(0) = 3$ to find $K\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =3 \\\\ K{e}^{5\\cdot 0} & =3 \\\\ K & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $y' = 5y$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=3$ is\n\n$$\ny = 3 e^{5x}  \\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/example-540.json" "file_sha256" "1a22bc19e61aacd899d91e4ef567556882bdb4398e2c495b8915566861d8da32"} {"question" "e-541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\cos(3y)\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} + \\sin(2x) = 0$ given that  $y\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0.$ Assume that $-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} < y < \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/example-541.json" "file_sha256" "a5f3e5f03f387c5a545cbc855fc0d68f5d920decc385e2d02bac45f56f99b312"} {"question" "e-541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\,\\text{d}y & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+C \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+{C}_{1}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C_1=3C.$\n\nNow let's apply the condition $y\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0$ to find $C_1\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+{C}_{1} \\\\ 0 & =0+{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\sin(3y)   =  \\dfrac {3} {2} \\cos(2x)\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037336/example-541.json" "file_sha256" "a5f3e5f03f387c5a545cbc855fc0d68f5d920decc385e2d02bac45f56f99b312"}] "usage" {"q-50220" [] "q-79425" [] "e-541" [] "e-540" []} "basis" 1261 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186290369 17592186290370 17592186290371 17592186290372 17592186290373 17592186292431 17592186292432 17592186292433 17592186292434 17592186292435] "immutable_fields" [[17592186290368 :answer-field/correct] [17592186290368 :answer-fiel